---
description: Type-only modules use the .t.ts suffix
globs: **/*.ts,**/*.tsx,**/*.t.ts
alwaysApply: true
---

# Type-only files are `*.t.ts`

A module that exports **only types** (no runtime values) uses the
`*.t.ts` suffix. Import it as `./name.t` (same as `form.t.ts`,
`Recursive.t.ts`, demo `*DemoTypes.t.ts`).

Do **not** leave a types-only walk/ctx/bag in a `.ts` file — that
extension means the module has runtime code.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — types only, but looks like a runtime module
// reviewWalk.ts
export type ReviewWalk<…> = { … };

// ✅ GOOD
// reviewWalk.t.ts
export type ReviewWalk<…> = { … };
import type { ReviewWalk } from "./reviewWalk.t";
```

`types.ts` as a package’s public type barrel is the existing exception
when that file is already the module’s type entry (e.g.
`section-review/types.ts`). New type-only splits still use `*.t.ts`.
